1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,963
OrderAnchor helps dream DEX Perps developers recover uncertain transactions by the

2
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:10,288
original hash, inspect the order outcome, and export verifiable evidence.

3
00:00:10,288 --> 00:00:15,287
The interface shows two completed testnet cycles: normal placement and cancellation,

4
00:00:15,287 --> 00:00:20,645
and recovery after locally injected response loss and process termination.

5
00:00:20,645 --> 00:00:26,405
The crash journal records the signed transaction before sending, then an unknown outcome.

6
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:30,720
After restart, the original hash was recovered without another placement.

7
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,827
Cancellation completed the recorded cycle.

8
00:00:33,827 --> 00:00:37,467
Now we click Recover via R P C.

9
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:41,829
This reads transactions, canonical receipts, order state, and historical nonces.

10
00:00:41,829 --> 00:00:44,960
It sends no new transaction.

11
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:49,480
The fresh result confirms cancellation with zero filled and remaining quantity.

12
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,466
The placement hash is unchanged.

13
00:00:51,466 --> 00:00:57,183
No additional mined signer transaction was found within this cycle's block interval.

14
00:00:57,183 --> 00:01:02,684
Export J S O N downloads portable public evidence for one operation.

15
00:01:02,684 --> 00:01:05,360
Export both cycles includes both demonstrations.

16
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:10,770
Neither export includes private keys or broadcastable signed transaction bytes.

17
00:01:10,770 --> 00:01:15,832
The downloaded bundle can be checked independently without the private database.

18
00:01:15,832 --> 00:01:17,618
Its checksum detects changes.

19
00:01:17,618 --> 00:01:23,927
The verifier checks transaction identity, receipts, order events, and scoped nonce history.

20
00:01:23,927 --> 00:01:26,000
OrderAnchor is available on GitHub.

21
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,233
This edited walkthrough uses real app captures and read only recovery.

22
00:01:30,233 --> 00:01:32,541
The original fault was injected locally.

23
00:01:32,541 --> 00:01:37,724
No new orders or cancellations were sent while making this demo.
